<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">York River (Virginia)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a> River is a tidal estuary in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, formed by the junction of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamunkey">Pamunkey</a> and Mattaponi rivers and flowing about 55 kilometres into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chesapeake-bay">Chesapeake Bay</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/werowocomoco">Werowocomoco</a>, the seat of the Powhatan paramount chief, stood on its north bank, and Yorktown, where the decisive siege of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a> ended in 1781, lies near its mouth.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/york-river-virginia.jpg" alt="York River (Virginia)" width="320" height="251" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: …trialsanderrors · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flickr_-_%E2%80%A6trialsanderrors_-_Yorktown_harbor,_Virginia,_1903.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
